# Structural config (decoder_type + op flags) locked in by section 1 of the
# revised experiment plan (1b: max-unpool verification, 1c: special-op
# ablation, both on O4 -- the Original-derived reference pick, see
# best_model.env and foundation_log.md's "Plan revision 2" section) --
# sourced by every downstream job in section 2/3
# (pruning_2a_grid_array.job, pruning_2b_fi_tune_array.job,
# postpruning_3a_quant_array.job) so it's edited in exactly one place once
# 1c's real results land, not duplicated per job script.
#
# Supersedes the original stage_1b/stage_2-era version of this file (still
# referenced by the now-superseded stage1b_structure_array.job /
# stage2_grid_array.job / stage2_4_fi_reduction_array.job /
# early_probe_p2_array.job -- kept for history, not part of the active plan).
#
# UPDATE THESE after 1c (compression/slurm/pre_pruning_1c_specialop_array.job)
# completes and collect_results.py has written its 5 rows to results.csv:
#   - ENET_DECODER_TYPE: 1b quantifies the Dice cost of upsample_conv vs
#     max_unpool on a symmetric O4 variant, but the choice itself is
#     structurally forced regardless of that number -- the section 2a grid's
#     filter axis (O2/O4/O8/O16/OF) has f5 != f_i for every entry except a
#     symmetric special case, which max_unpool cannot build (see
#     foundation_log.md finding #2). Only change this if the filter axis
#     itself gets redefined to stay symmetric.
#   - ENET_USE_DILATED/ASYMMETRIC/STRIDED: per 1c's "does it earn its
#     params/FLOP cost" ablation on O4. Defaults below (all 1) mean "keep
#     everything" -- the safe/unexamined starting point, not a real
#     decision yet.
#   - ENET_USE_DSC: 1c-iii probes DSC as an alternative to the three
#     special ops, but it is NOT carried into section 2a's grid by default
#     (2a's axis is filters x bottleneck-depth patterns only) -- only flip
#     this to 1 if 1c's results show DSC is worth carrying forward, as a
#     deliberate choice, not an automatic one.

export ENET_DECODER_TYPE="upsample_conv"
export ENET_USE_DILATED=1
export ENET_USE_ASYMMETRIC=1
export ENET_USE_STRIDED=1
export ENET_USE_DSC=0
